# Seen once 04cea37b let the checker past `TimeWithZone.new` (time_with_zone.sake's formatted_offset, Rails'
# `utc? && alternate_utc_string || ActiveSupport::TimeZone.seconds_to_utc_offset(utc_offset, colon)`).
# `a && b || c` with a Boolean `a` is typed `true|false | String`: the `||` does not drop the false that `a && b`
# can give, so String.sub rejects it ("argument 3 must be String|Hash, but can be true|false").
# Ruby: false && x is false, false || c is c: the value is always a String here; this prints "12:00Z".
# Not caused by 04cea37b. Workaround in the port: `return alternate_utc_string if utc?(t) && alternate_utc_string`.
def off(utc, alt = nil) = utc && alt || "+09:00"
p(String.sub("12:00+09:00", /\+09:00\z/, off(true, "Z")))
